## Summary

I authored complete **XCUITest UI coverage** for the TeslaSync Apple app (P4·P9·0002) and **proved it executes green on both Apple idioms**, then reached an honest **STATUS=BLOCKED** because the iOS/macOS `build test` gate is broken by a **pre-existing predecessor defect** outside this task's scope.

**Delivered (committed `013960080`, 14 files, +1248 lines, zero predecessor files touched):**
- **29 new test methods** across 3 idiom-aware suites + shared helpers:
  - `ComponentGalleryUITests` (13) — component states + loading/empty/error+retry/success/stale page-parity contract
  - `NavigationShellUITests` (9) — split (sidebar+detail) vs tab nav, pending routes, command palette, sidebar search, More tab, web-alias deep links, Settings
  - `AccessibilityUITests` (7) — Accessibility-XXXL Dynamic Type, alternate locale, accessible chart/map summaries, hit-target
- **~1000-LOC component gallery harness** (`Sources/Dev/`) — launch-arg-gated like the shipping demo views, real `Components/*` (ui/charts/data-display/feedback/forms/maps/motion), deterministic in-memory fixtures
- **Additive accessibility identifiers** on the real shell, command palette, settings + 2 launch args (`-uiTestComponentGallery`, `-uiTestDeepLink`)

**Verified (real output):**
- Full UI bundle **EXECUTED GREEN**: iPhone 16 (tab) **41 passed**, iPad Pro 11″ (split) **41 passed** — all 7 suites, both idioms
- Host gates: `swiftlint --strict`=0, `swiftformat --lint`=0 (0/4065), placeholder=0
- Found + fixed 2 real test defects via execution (command-palette multi-match element; sidebar icon-vs-text tap + iPad sidebar scroll)

**Why BLOCKED (not my code):** The consolidated baseline doesn't compile — pre-existing duplicate public types (`RecentDrives*`/`StateTimeline*`/`KioskClockPosition`) and ≥31 non-escaping-closure errors across untouched P4/P7 parity surfaces (`git status` confirms I changed none) → `IOS_EXIT=65`. macOS additionally has **0 dev-cert signing identities** (ADR-012) → `MAC_EXIT=65`. Fixing the broad predecessor refactor is a P4/P7 responsibility, so I proved my deliverable via a clean, reverted `Sources/`-only diagnostic rather than bypassing the predecessor. Full evidence in `.github/prompts/monorepo/logs/p4-p9-0002-xcuitest-ui.log` (ends `EXIT=65 / STATUS=BLOCKED`).

